    "q-126880": {
      "dom_id": "step-q126880",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14131939/assets/65047f9bf4f035000175fc55ee3ba6eeb4aa7ec39674a1984b95ba98a3f754f6.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{∂D}8y\\,dx+13x\\,dy,$ where $D$ is the region shown above.",
      "worked_solution": "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=8y$ and $Q(x,y)=13x.$ So,  \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=8,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=13.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}8y\\,dx+13x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(13-8)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}5\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =5\\,{∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =5\\cdot (\\frac{6\\cdot 6}{2}-{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =5\\cdot (18-4) \\\\  & =70.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
